<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
    <PropertyGroup>
        <GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
        <PackageId>ValkeyDotNet</PackageId>
        <Version>1.1.0</Version>
        <Description>A .NET client library for Valkey</Description>
        <Authors>Aleksandr Pavlov</Authors>
        <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 Aleksandr Pavlov</Copyright>
        <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/kidoz/valkey-dotnet</PackageProjectUrl>
        <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/kidoz/valkey-dotnet</RepositoryUrl>
        <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
        <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
        <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
        <PackageReleaseNotes>Adds a dedicated RESP2/RESP3 Pub/Sub subscriber with optional recovery, sharded Pub/Sub and a cluster subscriber, a standalone RESP3 client-tracking client, a bounded standalone connection owner, structured Lua scripting, isolated per-operation deadlines with explicit delivery status, opt-in owner telemetry, and lower bulk-reply parsing allocations.</PackageReleaseNotes>
        <PackageTags>valkey;redis;resp;cache;database</PackageTags>
        <!--
      Suppressions for AnalysisLevel=latest-all. Each is a deliberate design decision;
      do not extend this list without recording the reason here.
        1591    Undocumented public members are allowed; behaviour-bearing ones are documented.
        CA1720  RESP uses Integer and Double as canonical wire-type names.
        CA1003  PushReceived is Action<RespValue>, not EventHandler<T>: a push frame is a
                lightweight callback and an EventArgs wrapper would add a public type for no gain.
        CA1008  ValkeyProtocol values mirror the wire numbers (Resp2 = 2, Resp3 = 3). A zero
                'None' member would be meaningless and would break that mapping.
        CA1031  ReadNonPushAsync deliberately swallows user push-callback exceptions so a caller
                bug cannot desynchronize the wire. Connection-owner background attempts settle
                shared tasks and observe abandoned failures instead of leaking unobserved tasks.
                OwnerDiagnostics isolates instrument publication, sampling, measurement, and activity
                listener exceptions so telemetry never replaces a command's result or failure.
        CA1032  Exception constructors are intentionally constrained: ValkeyServerException derives
                ErrorCode from the message, and ValkeyConnectionException always wraps an inner cause.
        CA1065  ValkeyArgument implicit conversions throw on null instead of silently encoding an
                empty argument, which would send a different command than the caller wrote.
        CA1815  ValkeyArgument is a transient write-only argument wrapper; value equality over
                ReadOnlyMemory<byte> would be misleading.
        CA2000  ConnectAsync transfers ownership of the client to the caller and disposes it on
                every failure path.
        CA2213  The coordination primitives — _writeGate, _pendingCapacity, and _readerShutdown on
                ValkeyClient, _clientGate on ValkeyClusterClient, and _shutdown on
                ValkeyConnectionOwner — are deliberately not
                disposed. Invalidation runs while other callers may still be waiting on those
                gates and while the response loop still observes _readerShutdown.Token; disposing
                them would throw ObjectDisposedException over the terminal failure each pending
                caller is meant to observe. These types hold no unmanaged resource here:
                SemaphoreSlim allocates one only if AvailableWaitHandle is read, which these types
                never do, and these shutdown sources never schedule a cancellation timer.
        CA2225  Named alternates (FromString, FromInt32, ...) would enlarge the public surface;
                the implicit conversions are the intended ergonomics.
        CA5350  ValkeyScript uses SHA1 solely for the EVALSHA identifier mandated by Valkey's
                protocol, never for authentication, integrity, or any other security decision.
    -->
        <NoWarn>$(NoWarn);1591;CA1720;CA1003;CA1008;CA1031;CA1032;CA1065;CA1815;CA2000;CA2213;CA2225;CA5350</NoWarn>
    </PropertyGroup>
    <ItemGroup>
        <None Include="../../README.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
        <None Include="../../CHANGELOG.md" Pack="true" PackagePath="/" />
    </ItemGroup>
</Project>
